                  "title": "Holiday Calendar & Observance",
                  "section": "2",
                  "section_heading": "US Company Holidays (Denver, Austin, Seattle)",
                  "text": "These are the observed US company holidays. Where the holiday's actual date falls on a weekend, the actual date is shown in brackets.\nHoliday | 2026 (observed) | 2027 (observed)\nNew Year's Day | Thursday, January 1, 2026 | Friday, January 1, 2027\nMemorial Day | Monday, May 25, 2026 | Monday, May 31, 2027\nJuneteenth | Friday, June 19, 2026 | Friday, June 18, 2027 (actual June 19)\nIndependence Day | Friday, July 3, 2026 (actual July 4) | Monday, July 5, 2027 (actual July 4)\nLabor Day | Monday, September 7, 2026 | Monday, September 6, 2027\nVeterans Day | Wednesday, November 11, 2026 | Thursday, November 11, 2027\nThanksgiving Day | Thursday, November 26, 2026 | Thursday, November 25, 2027\nDay after Thanksgiving | Friday, November 27, 2026 | Friday, November 26, 2027\nChristmas Day | Friday, December 25, 2026 | Friday, December 24, 2027 (actual December 25)\nUS offices are open on Martin Luther King Jr. Day, Presidents' Day and Columbus Day / Indigenous Peoples' Day; they are not US company holidays. Employees who want to mark them can use a floating holiday (\u00a74).",
